#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# second_order_cone_optimization

#% text
# `second_order_cone_optimization(f, cons, vars)` gives the point that minimizes the linear function `f` under linear constraints and second-order cone constraints `norm(...) <= t`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A constraint `norm([x, y]) <= t` is read as `x^2 + y^2 <= t^2` with `t >= 0`; quadratic constraints `x^2 + y^2 <= r` are accepted as they are.

#% item
# A fourth argument selects the result as for `quadratic_optimization`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
second_order_cone_optimization(x + y, norm([x, y]) <= 1, [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> (-1/2)*2^(1/2), y -> (-1/2)*2^(1/2)]

#% cell
second_order_cone_optimization(x + y, [norm([x, y]) <= 1, y >= 0], [x, y], "PrimalMinimumValue")
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
second_order_cone_optimization(x + y, [x^2 + y^2 <= 1, (x - 1/2)^2 + y^2 <= 1], [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> (1/2)*(1 - 2^(1/2)), y -> (-1/2)*2^(1/2)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
